INT. GRAND HOTEL - HONEYMOON SUITE - MORNING

A fat canopy bed buried in pink pillows. Champagne bucket tipped over. A parrot on a brass stand.

HARRIGAN "HARRY" FOSTER-WELLS (50s, bathrobe, one slipper) staggers from the bathroom clutching a toothbrush. His new wife GWENDOLYN (40s, silk turban) shrieks from the bed, flings a pillow, and knocks the champagne bucket into the parrot's cage. Her sister MILDRED PETTIBONE (60s, stern, steaming iron in hand) bursts in through the connecting door, ignoring both of them, while the bellhop LIONEL (20s, brass buttons) wheels in a breakfast cart with a cheerful whistle.

He trips on the cart. It careens across the room. She leaps aside. He catches it. The parrot lands on his head.

                    PARROT
          (squawking)
          Congratulations!

                    HARRY
          Get it off!

                    GWENDOLYN
          Don't hurt Percival!

                    MILDRED
          I told you not to marry him.

                    LIONEL
          Breakfast, sir!

Harry spins. The parrot flaps. The toothbrush flies. It hits the iron. The iron hits the bucket. A fountain of ice erupts.

                    GWENDOLYN
          Harry, the pearls!

                    HARRY
          What pearls?

                    LIONEL
          The pearls on the tray, sir.

Everyone looks at the tray. On a silver plate, beside the croissants, sits a double strand of pearls.

                    MILDRED
          (grimly)
          I'll take those.

She plucks them. He bows. She exits through the connecting door, slamming it. The parrot settles on Harry's shoulder and preens.

                    PARROT
          Till death!
